ProsperoSunshine: the GameStream servers take no request bodies and keep serving after an error on one connection

Anyone who reaches TCP 47989 (the internet too, once the ports are forwarded) could stop the host with one request: a
chunked body cut off inside a chunk made Simple-Web-Server throw out of the io thread (its patch 0002 has the cause). Before
patch 0029 that ended the process with std::terminate; with it, accept_and_run logged and stopped the host cleanly, which
is as much of an off switch.
- Both servers refuse request bodies (accept_content = false): every GameStream request is a GET without one. This also
  takes away the 300 s a connection could wait for an announced body.
- Both servers set an on_error that does nothing, in case Simple-Web-Server calls it unchecked somewhere else.
- accept_and_run stops the host only when the server never got to accept (the port could not be bound, as upstream meant
  it). An exception after that comes out of a connection's callback: it is logged and the io_context runs on.

